        "number 22 belongs to PM10, not PM2.5"
      ],
      "text_sr": "Odbijena formulacija (EN): Observer's and Skeptic's readings for Leštane, Mostar, Mirijevo, and Vračar no longer hold in the source-labelled hour ending 23:00 UTC (our estimate of true UTC is 22:00) [F3]. The highest measured PM10 value moved from 73 to 45 µg/m³ [F5] and PM2.5 from 70 to 42 µg/m³ [F9], placing both maxima at Zeleno brdo across 30 stations while Krnjača holds the lowest values for both fractions at 22 and 21 µg/m³ [F4][F8]. Over the same hour, the highest measured NO2 value moved from 35 to 43 µg/m³ at Bulevar despota Stefana across 31 stations [F6][F7], meaning both the particle peak at Zeleno brdo and the NO2 peak at Bulevar despota Stefana now sit at stations where about 28 thousand people live within 1 km, whereas Krnjača has about 11 thousand people within 1 km [F45][F46][F48].",
      "text_en": "Observer's and Skeptic's readings for Leštane, Mostar, Mirijevo, and Vračar no longer hold in the source-labelled hour ending 23:00 UTC (our estimate of true UTC is 22:00) [F3]. The highest measured PM10 value moved from 73 to 45 µg/m³ [F5] and PM2.5 from 70 to 42 µg/m³ [F9], placing both maxima at Zeleno brdo across 30 stations while Krnjača holds the lowest values for both fractions at 22 and 21 µg/m³ [F4][F8]. Over the same hour, the highest measured NO2 value moved from 35 to 43 µg/m³ at Bulevar despota Stefana across 31 stations [F6][F7], meaning both the particle peak at Zeleno brdo and the NO2 peak at Bulevar despota Stefana now sit at stations where about 28 thousand people live within 1 km, whereas Krnjača has about 11 thousand people within 1 km [F45][F46][F48].",
